              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Cultural Events In "
            },
            {
              "_key": "pvjxmh8o5h31",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "9ixqd8rcaecu"
              ],
              "text": "Luxor"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "9ixqd8rcaecu",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Luxor, with its rich historical and cultural landscape, also celebrates various events and festivals that add color and vibrancy to the city. Here are some notable events in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Luxor"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ":"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luxor",
              "newTab": true
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Moulid of Abu al-Haggag"
            },
            {
              "_key": "8d3b2nfps9pb",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ": Celebrated in honor of Luxor’s patron saint, Yousef Abu al-Haggag, this festival is one of Egypt’s largest. It takes place around the Mosque of Abu al-Haggag, built atop "
            },
            {
              "_key": "ay9zqn3mc99n",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "raovtxm7dlhh"
              ],
              "text": "Luxor Temple"
            },
            {
              "_key": "xqg8pl8yhaqz",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". Occurring in the third week before Ramadan, this five-day carnival features traditional music, dancing, and various "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000009"
              ],
              "text": "cultural"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " activities, reflecting the rich heritage of the region."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/are-there-crocodiles-in-the-nile-river/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/nairu-gawa-ni-wani-wa-iru-no-ka",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "raovtxm7dlhh",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.the-luxor-temple",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Luxor Marathon"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ": Usually held in late January or early February, this marathon is a significant athletic "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000f"
              ],
              "text": "event"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". The race course winds through the West Bank, starting and finishing at Deir al-Bahri, and encompasses major archaeological sites. It attracts runners from around the world, providing a unique backdrop of ancient monuments."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/home/dahab-historical-guide-4/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/dahab/dahab-historical-guide",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000015",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000013",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Local Moulids"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ": Several smaller moulids (celebrations of saints) occur around Luxor, each with its unique charm. These include the moulids of Abu’l Gumsan near Tariff, Sheikh Musa and Abu al-Jud in Karnak, Sheikh Hamid, and Sheikh Hussein. These events offer an authentic glimpse into local religious and cultural practices."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Moulid of Mar Girgis (St George)"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ": This week-long "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000018"
              ],
              "text": "Coptic"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " festival is held at the Mar Girgis Monastery in Razagat, culminating on November 11. Despite being in a restricted area for foreigners, it draws large crowds for its religious significance and cultural festivities."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/the-copts-of-egypt-guardians-of-an-ancient-faith/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/ejiputo-no-koputo-kyoto",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Conclusion"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "These events in Luxor not only provide entertainment but also a deeper understanding of the local customs, religious beliefs, and communal spirit. They offer an excellent opportunity for visitors to engage with the local community and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001f"
              ],
              "text": "experience"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000021",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " the true essence of Luxor beyond its ancient ruins and temples."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/home/dahab-historical-guide-8/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
